# PathWise Project Rules

## Architecture & Conflict Prevention
- Always inspect existing models, migrations, and controllers before creating new features to prevent naming collisions or duplicate logic.
- Reuse existing FormRequests, middleware, and database traits across Laravel controllers rather than writing redundant code.

## Comments & Documentation
- Document complex business logic, custom database queries, and non-obvious algorithm steps using clear inline comments.
- Add concise docblocks to Laravel controller methods and custom Vue component props, events, and computed properties.

## UI/UX Consistency & Design Elements
- Maintain consistent spacing, typography scales, and responsive design patterns using the established Tailwind configuration.
- You are permitted to create new design elements or components when building new features, provided they strictly match the style, color palette, and layout conventions of existing components.

## Validation & Data Integrity
- Implement strict dual-layer validation: Laravel FormRequests on the backend and corresponding reactive validation on the frontend.
- Explicitly check for uniqueness and duplicate entries at the database and model levels (e.g., unique composite keys for courses and departments).

## Token Efficiency & Tool Usage
- Avoid broad wildcard directory searches (`*`). Use precise, targeted file paths for all read and search tool calls.
- Read only the specific files required for the active task; never scan vendor, storage, or build directories.

## Terminal & Environment
- Operating System: Windows (PowerShell)
- Note: Never use `&&` to chain commands in PowerShell. Use semicolons (`;`) or run commands on separate lines instead.

## Allowed Packages & Dependencies
- Do not use Laravel Flux, Livewire Pro, or any paid/proprietary packages that require a license key. Stick strictly to standard open-source tools, Tailwind, Blade, and Vue.

## Objectives for pathwise
- Course Creation
- AI-Powered Course Recommendation
- Quiz Generation
- Output Evaluation
- Certificate Generation
- Payment Tracking
- Performance Tracking and Analytics Report Generation